{
  "sentences": [
    {
      "i": 0,
      "revised": "Nowadays, transport is a very important issue in many countries.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "原句缺少冠词和名词单复数错误（many country），且“problem”搭配不当，改为“issue”更准确；添加逗号使句子更流畅。"
    },
    {
      "i": 1,
      "revised": "Some people think the government should spend money on public transport rather than building new roads.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "spelling", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "拼写错误（goverment），介词搭配错误（spend money for），动词形式错误（not for build），改为“spend money on”和“rather than building”更符合英语表达。"
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "revised": "I agree with this opinion to some extent but not entirely.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“I am agree”是语法错误，agree是动词，不需要be动词；表达“在某种程度上”用“to some extent”更地道。"
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "revised": "Firstly, public transport is beneficial for people.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“good for people”过于简单，改为“beneficial for people”更正式，符合学术写作风格。"
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "revised": "This is because many people do not have cars and they need buses and trains to go to work and school.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation", "spelling"],
      "explanation": "原句缺少主语和连接词，且“dont”缺少撇号，car和bus/train应为复数，go后需要介词to。修改后句子结构完整，语法正确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "revised": "If buses are better, people will use them more and there will be less traffic.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“more better”是双重比较级错误，改为“better”；“the traffic will be less”不自然，改为“there will be less traffic”更符合英语表达。"
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "revised": "In my city, buses are always late and very crowded, so people do not like to take them.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "spelling", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "bus和crowd需要复数形式，dont缺少撇号，添加逗号使句子更清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "revised": "Also, trains are too expensive for students.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "train和student应为复数，添加逗号使连接更自然。"
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "revised": "So the government should make it cheaper and faster.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "spelling", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "拼写错误（goverment），cheap和fast的比较级应为cheaper和faster，用“make it cheaper and faster”更简洁。"
    },
    {
      "i": 9,
      "revised": "Secondly, new roads are also important.",
      "tags": ["grammar"],
      "explanation": "road应为复数roads，与上下文一致。"
    },
    {
      "i": 10,
      "revised": "This is because the city is growing and more people buy cars every year.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "原句缺少主语和连接词，grow应为现在分词growing，car应为复数cars。"
    },
    {
      "i": 11,
      "revised": "If there are no new roads, traffic jams will be very bad and people will waste a lot of time.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "“no new road”应为复数roads，添加逗号使条件句更清晰，waste时态应与主句一致用将来时。"
    },
    {
      "i": 12,
      "revised": "For example, my father drives to work every day and he spends two hours on the road.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "drive和spend应为第三人称单数，hour应为复数hours，添加逗号使句子更流畅。"
    },
    {
      "i": 13,
      "revised": "This is very bad for him and for the economy as well.",
      "tags": ["vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "“also”改为“as well”更自然，避免与前面句子重复。"
    },
    {
      "i": 14,
      "revised": "But I think public transport is more important than roads.",
      "tags": ["grammar"],
      "explanation": "road应为复数roads，与上下文一致。"
    },
    {
      "i": 15,
      "revised": "This is because roads encourage more cars and more pollution.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary", "punctuation"],
      "explanation": "原句缺少主语和连接词，road应为复数roads，“make more car”表达不准确，改为“encourage more cars”更符合逻辑。"
    },
    {
      "i": 16,
      "revised": "Public transport can carry many people at one time and it is good for the environment.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "spelling", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "拼写错误（enviroment），去掉the使表达更通用，“in one time”改为“at one time”更准确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 17,
      "revised": "Also, if more people take buses, the city will be quieter and the air will be cleaner, so everybody can be healthier and happier.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "punctuation", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "bus应为复数buses，quiet、clean、healthy、happy的比较级应分别为quieter、cleaner、healthier、happier，添加逗号使句子更清晰。"
    },
    {
      "i": 18,
      "revised": "In conclusion, I think the government should spend more money on public transport but also build some roads when it is necessary.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "spelling", "collocation"],
      "explanation": "拼写错误（goverment），介词搭配错误（spend money for），road应为复数roads，改为“spend money on”更准确。"
    },
    {
      "i": 19,
      "revised": "Both are important for the people and the development of the country.",
      "tags": ["grammar", "vocabulary"],
      "explanation": "Both作主语时谓语用复数are，country develop应改为名词短语“the development of the country”更符合语法。"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "最频繁的问题包括：主谓一致和名词单复数错误（如many country, road应为roads）、介词搭配不当（spend money for）、拼写错误（goverment, enviroment）以及比较级使用错误（more better）。这些基础语法错误严重影响了句子的准确性和得分。"
}

{
  "essay": "In many countries, transport has become a serious problem. Some people believe that governments should spend money on improving public transport rather than building new roads. I partly agree with this view: public transport deserves the larger share of investment, but new roads are still necessary in some situations.\n\nThe first reason to prioritise public transport is that many people do not own a car and depend on buses and trains to get to work or school. If buses were more reliable and comfortable, more people would use them, and traffic congestion would decrease. In my city, buses are often late and extremely crowded, so many residents avoid them, while train fares are too high for students. Governments should therefore make public transport cheaper, faster and more dependable.\n\nHowever, building new roads also matters. Cities are growing and more people buy cars every year. Without new roads, traffic jams would become severe and people would waste hours commuting. For example, my father drives to work every day and spends two hours on the road, which harms both his well-being and the economy. In such cases, additional roads can ease pressure on the network.\n\nNevertheless, I believe public transport is more important overall. New roads tend to encourage more car use and therefore more pollution, whereas a single bus or train can carry many passengers at once and is better for the environment. If more people took public transport, cities would be quieter, the air would be cleaner, and everyone would be healthier and happier.\n\nIn conclusion, although new roads are sometimes necessary, I believe governments should allocate more funding to public transport, while building roads only where they are genuinely needed. Both are important for people and for the development of the country.",
  "original_addresses_question": true,
  "answers": [
    {
      "part": "表明立场：部分同意，公共交通应获更多投资，但新路在必要时仍需建设",
      "quote": "I partly agree with this view: public transport deserves the larger share of investment, but new roads are still necessary in some situations."
    },
    {
      "part": "论述支持公共交通的理由（无车人群依赖、改善服务可减少拥堵）",
      "quote": "If buses were more reliable and comfortable, more people would use them, and traffic congestion would decrease."
    },
    {
      "part": "论述建设新路的必要性（城市扩张、汽车增多、通勤时间）",
      "quote": "Without new roads, traffic jams would become severe and people would waste hours commuting."
    },
    {
      "part": "解释为何总体而言公共交通更重要（环保、载客量大）",
      "quote": "New roads tend to encourage more car use and therefore more pollution, whereas a single bus or train can carry many passengers at once and is better for the environment."
    },
    {
      "part": "结论重申立场：更多资金给公共交通，道路仅在真正需要时建设",
      "quote": "In conclusion, although new roads are sometimes necessary, I believe governments should allocate more funding to public transport, while building roads only where they are genuinely needed."
    }
  ],
  "key_changes": [
    "将开头段改为直接回应题目并明确立场：用 \"I partly agree with this view: public transport deserves the larger share of investment, but new roads are still necessary in some situations.\" 替换原来含糊的 \"I am agree with this opinion in some way but not all.\"，同时修正语法错误。",
    "修正原文大量基础语法错误，例如将 \"goverment\" 改为 \"governments\"、\"dont\" 改为 \"do not\"、\"more better\" 改为 \"more reliable and comfortable\"、\"very crowd\" 改为 \"extremely crowded\"，并统一使用现在时和条件句。",
    "将第二段中零散的理由整合为因果链：用 \"If buses were more reliable and comfortable, more people would use them, and traffic congestion would decrease.\" 把\"公交好→更多人用→交通减少\"的逻辑写清楚。",
    "将第三段关于新路的论述改为更具体的论证：用 \"Without new roads, traffic jams would become severe and people would waste hours commuting.\" 替换原来较口语化的 \"If there is no new road the traffic jam will be very bad and people waste a lot of time.\"，并保留父亲的例子但修正时态和表达。",
    "将第四段的环境论点改写为对比结构：用 \"New roads tend to encourage more car use and therefore more pollution, whereas a single bus or train can carry many passengers at once and is better for the environment.\" 使公共交通与道路的对比更清晰。",
    "重写结论段，使其与全文立场一致并避免绝对化：用 \"In conclusion, although new roads are sometimes necessary, I believe governments should allocate more funding to public transport, while building roads only where they are genuinely needed.\" 替换原来较简单的总结。"
  ],
  "band_rationale": "本次改写针对 Band 7 目标，在四项标准上做了以下调整：任务回应方面，开头段明确给出\"部分同意\"的立场，并在主体段分别讨论公共交通的优点、新路的必要性以及为何公共交通总体更重要，结论再次呼应立场，使全文论证完整。连贯与衔接方面，使用 \"The first reason\"、\"However\"、\"Nevertheless\"、\"In conclusion\" 等连接词，段落主题句清晰，每段围绕一个中心论点展开。词汇资源方面，替换了原文中的口语化表达和拼写错误，使用 \"reliable and comfortable\"、\"traffic congestion\"、\"commuting\"、\"allocate more funding\" 等更准确的学术词汇，同时避免过度堆砌。语法范围与准确性方面，修正了主谓一致、时态、冠词和比较级等错误，并引入条件句和对比结构，使句子更复杂且准确。需要说明的是，以上只是朝着 Band 7 目标所做的修改方向，并不表示这篇改写已经达到或被评为任何分数。"
}

