{
  "essay": "In many cities, traffic congestion has become a serious problem, and governments must decide how to use limited budgets. Some people argue that money should go to public transport instead of new roads. I largely agree with this view, although I believe some road building is still necessary.\n\nThe main reason to invest in public transport is that it can move a large number of people efficiently. A single train can carry hundreds of passengers, while the same number of people would need hundreds of cars. If buses and trains are frequent, cheap and reliable, many drivers will choose them, which will reduce traffic jams. For example, after my city opened a new metro line, the main road to the city centre became much less crowded during rush hour. This shows that good public transport can persuade people to leave their cars at home.\n\nAnother advantage is the environment. Cars produce a lot of air pollution and carbon emissions, which are harmful to people's health and contribute to climate change. Public transport produces less pollution per passenger, so it is a more sustainable option in the long term. Investing in buses and trains therefore helps cities to meet their environmental targets.\n\nOn the other hand, new roads are sometimes needed. In rural areas, there are not enough passengers to make train lines profitable, so people depend on cars. Also, goods are mostly transported by trucks, and poor roads can slow down the economy. In these cases, road building is essential.\n\nIn conclusion, I agree that governments should give priority to public transport because it is more efficient and better for the environment. However, they should still build roads in places where public transport is not practical.",
  "original_addresses_question": true,
  "answers": [
    {
      "part": "表明立场：主要同意投资公共交通，但认为仍需建设部分道路",
      "quote": "I largely agree with this view, although I believe some road building is still necessary."
    },
    {
      "part": "论证公共交通的效率优势（运载量大、减少拥堵）",
      "quote": "The main reason to invest in public transport is that it can move a large number of people efficiently."
    },
    {
      "part": "论证公共交通的环境优势",
      "quote": "Public transport produces less pollution per passenger, so it is a more sustainable option in the long term."
    },
    {
      "part": "承认建设新道路的必要性（农村和货运）",
      "quote": "In rural areas, there are not enough passengers to make train lines profitable, so people depend on cars."
    },
    {
      "part": "结论重申立场：优先公共交通，但在不实用处建路",
      "quote": "In conclusion, I agree that governments should give priority to public transport because it is more efficient and better for the environment."
    }
  ],
  "key_changes": [
    "将开头立场句从“I mostly agree with this view”改为“I largely agree with this view”，使语气更正式、更符合学术写作。",
    "在第二段例子后增加解释句“This shows that good public transport can persuade people to leave their cars at home.”，加强论点与例子的逻辑联系。",
    "在第三段末尾增加“Investing in buses and trains therefore helps cities to meet their environmental targets.”，进一步拓展环境优势的论证。",
    "在第四段末尾增加“In these cases, road building is essential.”，使让步段与主立场衔接更紧密。",
    "将结论段中“However, they should still build roads in places where public transport is not practical.”保留，但整体段落划分更清晰，每段一个中心。"
  ],
  "band_rationale": "任务回应：立场明确且贯穿全文，对公共交通的效率、环境优势及道路建设的必要性均有讨论，例子得到解释，结论呼应开头。连贯与衔接：段落主题清晰，增加了解释性句子和过渡句，逻辑连接更自然。词汇资源：使用了“largely”“persuade”“sustainable”“environmental targets”等恰当词汇，避免重复。语法多样性与准确性：修正了原文中可能存在的轻微错误，增加了复合句和连接词，句式更丰富。整体向Band 7要求靠拢，但未对分数做出任何声称。"
}

